+Spatial Hierarchies organize data into tree structures to accelerate point location via recursive search [S1, unofficial]. They solve the problem of inefficient traversal in sparse scenes by reducing intersection tests [G]. Unlike sibling methods such as [Hierarchical Spatial Enumeration Optimization](1663-hierarchical-spatial-enumeration-optimization.md) or [Jiang et al. Acceleration Structure](1673-jiang-et-al-acceleration-structure.md), they dynamically partition space rather than relying on fixed grids or image-order traversal.
