 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Insertion into Spatial Hierarchies](13180-insertion-into-spatial-hierarchies.md)
-Algorithmic process of adding primitives to a hierarchy. It solves the problem of maintaining spatial coherence in dynamic scenes. Unlike static build methods, it processes primitives incrementally, making it suitable for dynamic environments but sensitive to insertion order.
+Insertion into spatial hierarchies refers to the algorithmic process of adding primitives into an existing or growing hierarchical data structure. Unlike static build methods that analyze the entire scene at once, insertion methods process primitives one by one, allowing for incremental updates. This makes it suitable for dynamic environments, though it is highly sensitive to the order of insertion. It is chosen when scenes require frequent updates or when building from unsorted data [G].
 
